 Chancellor Merz is set to host Hungarian Prime Minister Magyar.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Neuer injury gives Urbig chance to shape Bayern and Germany future</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8b689b830b9c5f19a029dc3e754cd4e2eecf6afe9d2aa587630d2b78b64ef63</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T15:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042--b0a77bac4246.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/neuer-injury-gives-urbig-chance-to-shape-bayern-and-germany-future/a-79910042?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Manuel Neuer's latest injury gives Jonas Urbig a run of games in Bayern's goal. Marc-André ter Stegen remains Germany’s No. 1, but Urbig now has a chance to strengthen his case for the future.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Borussia Dortmund's Felix Nmecha and the question of religion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c21ec9fe244fd2daa7e3266756aa8055f6c3ccad461eec875013fc70537d7338</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-10T11:12:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432--cd7bb6e11389.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/borussia-dortmund-s-felix-nmecha-and-the-question-of-religion/a-79900432?maca=en-rss-en-ger-1023-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Felix Nmecha's "Crowns down" celebration has drawn criticism from a Borussia Dortmund fan club, reopening debate over faith, inclusion and religious messaging in football.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>37 years after fall of Berlin Wall: How divided are Germans?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d87251254fd35807e1f631b6551e81f017de6826e020f8cf6d794f8179b74860</id><updated>2026-11-11T16:22:18Z</updated><published>2026-11-09